cle, bypassing the limits of effort, form, and fatigue that hold most workouts back.\n\nThis isn't a shortcut to a sculpted lower body. But having the ability to fire your glutes at the exact intensity you choose — for hundreds of contractions per session — is a massive advantage traditional training can't match.\n\nThe results? In just one 20-minute session with the Ultra Glute Stimulator:\n\n✓ 600+ deep glute contractions, the equivalent of 3,000+ squats\n✓ Direct activation of the gluteus maximus and medius (the muscles that lift and shape)\n✓ Zero strain on your knees or lower back\n✓ Reaches deep muscle fibers most workouts never touch\n✓ Fully hands-free —train while you work, cook, or relax\n✓ No pads, no gels, no maintenance, ever\n\nNMES isn't some gimmick either. It's been studied for decades and endorsed by some of the world's leading researchers. As Dr. Toshio Moritani, Ph.D., a pioneer in NMES science, put it:\n\n\"The NMES offers a promising alternative to traditional strength training for enhancing the strength parameters and motor abilities described above. Because of the clear-cut advantages in time management, we can expect this method to see the increasing use in high-performance sports.\"\n\nThat same technology — trusted in clinical rehab and elite athletic training — is now engineered specifically for your glutes inside the Ultra Glute Stimulator.","caption":null,"linkUrl":"https://apebornfitness.com/products/nextgen-ultra-glute-stimulator","imageUrl":"https://scontent-lga3-2.xx.fbcdn.net/v/t39.35426-6/823153199_4500997836827764_1151637012327008276_n.jpg?_nc_cat=105&ccb=1-7&_nc_sid=c53f8f&_nc_ohc=QH9uX2ql4L4Q7kNvwHwobd3&_nc_oc=AdrcX8Pl-Z1Z2u89BZRGqJ31qt1FdqdIfG68raI0Pb2IHnTnZe7CPzoAISAHhcE_U9E&_nc_zt=14&_nc_ht=scontent-lga3-2.xx&_nc_gid=KAtc36otxCMlEdXH4WFHJA&_nc_ss=78180&oh=00_AQS7_a4jtE6AWU-HeNQJeAoKVscuUX3MSMaTO-E2W2aKbw&oe=6AF3C240","videoUrl":null},{"title":"SALE ENDS TODAY!","body":"If you want to lift and tone your glutes and you're not using NMES technology, you're at a serious disadvantage. Here's why.\n\nIt comes down to control. Neuromuscular Electrical Stimulation (NMES) gives you precise control over the intensity of every muscle contraction, something squats and lunges simply can't replicate.\n\nAnd I know NMES sounds like a buzzword, so let me break it down.\n\nYour muscles contract in response to electrical signals from your nerves. The stronger the signal, the more muscle fibers get recruited. NMES sends those signals directly into the muscle, bypassing the limits of effort, form, and fatigue that hold most workouts back.\n\nThis isn't a shortcut to a sculpted lower body. But having the ability to fire your glutes at the exact intensity you choose — for hundreds of contractions per session — is a massive advantage traditional training can't match.\n\nThe results? In just one 20-minute session with the Ultra Glute Stimulator:\n\n✓ 600+ deep glute contractions, the equivalent of 3,000+ squats\n✓ Direct activation of the gluteus maximus and medius (the muscles that lift and shape)\n✓ Zero strain on your knees or lower back\n✓ Reaches deep muscle fibers most workouts never touch\n✓ Fully hands-free —train while you work, cook, or relax\n✓ No pads, no gels, no maintenance, ever\n\nNMES isn't some gimmick either. It's been studied for decades and endorsed by some of the world's leading researchers. As Dr. Toshio Moritani, Ph.D., a pioneer in NMES science, put it:\n\n\"The NMES offers a promising alternative to traditional strength training for enhancing the strength parameters and motor abilities described above. Because of the clear-cut advantages in time management, we can expect this method to see the increasing use in high-performance sports.\"\n\nThat same technology — trusted in clinical rehab and elite athletic training — is now engineered specifically for your glutes inside the Ultra Glute Stimulator.","caption":null,"linkUrl":"https://apebornfitness.com/products/nextgen-ultra-glute-stimulator","imageUrl":"https://scontent-lga3-1.xx.fbcdn.net/v/t39.35426-6/821267759_1077738048504540_8191083547656699885_n.jpg?_nc_cat=103&ccb=1-7&_nc_sid=c53f8f&_nc_ohc=SJoLh0sm4woQ7kNvwGdSRw1&_nc_oc=Adq9mMidoApg2NQpVHm7GEHsPusOnc65xs5WTnx-FE3OZOrJUsoT4nz_oVTolQI_Tx0&_nc_zt=14&_nc_ht=scontent-lga3-1.xx&_nc_gid=KAtc36otxCMlEdXH4WFHJA&_nc_ss=78180&oh=00_AQQVZ3ty0yXL34lu3EkAiO8rtWv_VOGHUi-UYM8l91OqDw&oe=6AF3C87A","videoUrl":null}]},"brandedContent":null,"euTransparency":null},{"id":"919652531181278","adId":null,"url":"https://www.facebook.com/ads/library?id=919652531181278","page":{"id":"107382974280858","name":"Power Plate Beauty & Wellness","url":"https://www.facebook.com/powerplatehbw/","isDeleted":false,"profilePictureUrl":"https://scontent-lga3-1.xx.fbcdn.net/v/t39.35426-6/714424412_1634987738038264_5705897677996713206_n.jpg?stp=dst-jpg_s60x60_tt6&_nc_cat=103&ccb=1-7&_nc_sid=c53f8f&_nc_ohc=oBh1cwfDqQQQ7kNvwGNle6b&_nc_oc=AdpOkMarBdV9Fgz7uehippj5wub4EI5aC0IX02Z6O3oFy7YRLSmvUdYsH7IGSS8e5Ig&_nc_zt=14&_nc_ht=scontent-lga3-1.xx&_nc_gid=KAtc36otxCMlEdXH4WFHJA&_nc_ss=78180&oh=00_AQQfB-Px6jOW218QTIbyk9KbgwcQhW8rD1x7szdeQ7m2Tg&oe=6AF3C2CE","likeCount":37321,"categories":["Health & wellness website"]},"campaign":{"collationId":"766700126407231","collationCount":1},"isActive":true,"publisherPlatforms":["FACEBOOK","INSTAGRAM","AUDIENCE_NETWORK","MESSENGER","THREADS"],"startedAt":"2026-07-29T07:00:00.000Z","endedAt":"2026-11-06T08:00:00.000Z","categories":["UNKNOWN"],"countries":[],"impressions":{"text":null,"index":-1},"spend":null,"creative":{"bodyText":"There’s a reason so many people feel like they’re doing everything right—and still not seeing results.\n\n--They’ve been told to strengthen the pelvic floor.\n--They’ve been told to do Kegels.\n--They’ve been told consistency is the key.\n\nAnd yet:\n-The leaks still happen\n-The control doesn’t fully return\n-The progress feels slow, or nonexistent\n-At some point, the question shifts from “Am I doing this enough?” to something more fundamental:\n\n“Am I even doing the right thing?”\n\nBecause what if the issue isn’t strength at all?\n\nThe Pelvic Floor: A Muscle System You Can’t See (Or Easily Feel)\n\nThe pelvic floor is not a single muscle. It’s a coordinated system that supports:\n\nBladder control\nBowel function\nPelvic organ stability\nCore pressure and movement\n\nLike any muscle system, the muscles in this area respondsto training. But it has one critical difference:\n\nYou can’t see it. And most people can’t feel it clearly.\n\n==>> This creates a unique problem.\n\nWhy Traditional Pelvic Floor Training Breaks Down\n\nOn paper, pelvic floor therapy is straightforward:\n\nContract the muscles.\nRepeat the contraction.\nBuild strength over time.\n\nBut in practice, three things consistently go wrong:\n\n1) The muscles are hard to isolate\nPeople often recruit surrounding muscles instead—or push in the wrong direction.\n\n2) Activation is inconsistent\nWithout clear feedback, it’s difficult to know if you’re doing it correctly.\n\n3) Compliance drops off\nWhen results are unclear, people stop doing the work.\nSo the instruction becomes:\n“Squeeze.”\n\nBut without proper activation, that “squeeze” often doesn’t reach the muscles that actually matter.\n\nThis isn’t a discipline issue.\n\nIt’s a signal problem.\n\nThe Shift: From Trying to Activate… to Actually Activating\n\nIf the core issue is activation—not strength—then the solution changes.\n\nInstead of asking someone to contract a muscle they can’t feel…\n\nWhat if you could trigger this muscle group automatically?\n\nThis is where whole body vibration (WBV) comes into play—specifically 3D harmonic vibration from Power Plate. \n\nWhat Actually Happens on a Power Plate\n\nWhen you stand on a Power Plate in particular the body doesn’t just “shake.”\nA precise mechanical signal moves through the system, and the whole body.  \nMuscles are rapidly and subtly destabilized \nSensory receptors detect that destabilization \nThe nervous system responds with a reflex contraction\nThis is an automatic loop—no conscious effort required.\n\nAnd that reflex doesn’t stay local.\n\nIt travels through the entire neuromuscular system—including the pelvic floor.\n\nSo instead of trying to activate the muscle…     \n\nThe body activates it for you.\n\nWhat the Research Shows\nAcross multiple controlled trials studying whole body vibration and pelvic floor function, the findings are consistent:\nIncreased pelvic floor muscle activation\nImprovements in strength comparable to traditional pelvic floor training\nReduction in urinary incontinence severity\nMeasurable improvements in quality of life\nIn some cases, better outcomes than voluntary contraction alone\nNo evidence of fatigue in healthy individuals\nReports of restored continence in as little as six weeks in certain cases\n\nThe takeaway is simple:\n\nThis works because it activates muscles people struggle to activate on their own.\n\nThe Physiology, Without the Noise\nHere’s what’s happening at a basic level:\nVibration introduces a rapid, low-level destabilization \nMuscle sensors (spindles) detect that change\nA reflex signal is sent through the spinal cord\nThe brain responds by trigger a reflex response that contacts the muscle\nThe result:\nMore muscle fibers recruited\nBetter coordination\nStronger, more synchronized contractions\nAnd importantly, this includes the pelvic floor.\n\nThis Doesn’t Replace Therapy—It Makes It Work\nThere’s a misconception that new tools replace existing methods.\n\nIn reality, they fix the weak link.\n\nWhole body vibration doesn’t eliminate pelvic floor therapy.\n\nIt improves it by addressing the core issue: activation.\n\nUsed correctly, it becomes:\nA primer — turning the muscles “on” before training\nA multiplier — increasing activation during exercises\nA compliance tool — fast, simple, and easy to repeat\nInstead of asking someone to guess how to engage a muscle…\n\nYou give them a system that activates it, then build control on top of that.\nWhat This Looks Like in Practice (Notes For The Urologist)\nThe integration is straightforward.\n\nStep 1 — Activation\nStand on the platform with a slight bend in the knees\nGoal: reflexively engage the pelvic floor\n\nStep 2 — Add Intent\nLayer in a light voluntary contraction during vibration\nNow you get reflex activation plus conscious control\n\nStep 3 — Add Movement\nIntroduce simple positions:\nMini squats\nStatic holds\nFunctional stances\n\nStep 4 — Transition Off\nReinforce activation with traditional exercises\nNothing about the therapy changes.\n\nWhat changes is the quality of activation going into it.\n\nA Simple, Practical Protocol (That You Can Do In Private At Home)\n\nBased on commonly used clinical ranges:\nKnees slightly bent (20–40°)\nFrequency: ~20–40 Hz\nAmplitude: ~2–4 mm\n30–60 seconds per set\n3–5 sets\n2–5 sessions per week\nTotal time: ~5–10 minutes\nThis is not a long session.\nBut it delivers a dense, consistent stimulus.\nWho This Is For\nThis approach is especially relevant for:\nStress urinary incontinence\nPostpartum recovery\nAging populations\nPost-prostatectomy patients\nAnyone with weak pelvic floor muscles or poor neuromuscular control\nIn other words:\nPeople who have tried to “do the exercises”—and haven’t seen meaningful change.","title":"Bladder Control Isn’t a Strength Problem. It’s an Activation Problem (How Power Plate Helps)","caption":"powerplate.com","linkUrl":"https://www.powerplate.com/blogs/news/bladder-control-isn-t-a-strength-problem-it-s-an-activation-problem-how-power-plate-helps","linkDescription":"There’s a reason so many people feel like they’re doing everything right—and still not seeing results. They’ve been told to strengthen the pelvic floor. They’ve been told to do Kegels. They’ve been told consistency is the key. And yet: The leaks still happen The control doesn’t fully r...","callToAction":null,"callToActionType":null,"displayFormat":"IMAGE","images":[{"url":"https: