t-jpg_s60x60_tt6&_nc_cat=106&ccb=1-7&_nc_sid=c53f8f&_nc_ohc=PV4HdKlqq4QQ7kNvwH4lh2u&_nc_oc=Adq0eFTrVmzoAwgctzngAvHb3td4Daae5YPpxSm3VOlLTkAdkWvB6y-OW0op-KiTZYc&_nc_zt=14&_nc_ht=scontent-lga3-3.xx&_nc_gid=KAtc36otxCMlEdXH4WFHJA&_nc_ss=78180&oh=00_AQSixmxM_fBaQgoo8EcmS8X30zF3xqLhOEdN5wEhSXzbsQ&oe=6AF3E89B","likeCount":11,"categories":["Business","Sports Instruction"]},"campaign":{"collationId":"2103480173578879","collationCount":1},"isActive":true,"publisherPlatforms":["FACEBOOK","INSTAGRAM","AUDIENCE_NETWORK","MESSENGER"],"startedAt":"2026-09-04T07:00:00.000Z","endedAt":"2026-11-06T08:00:00.000Z","categories":["UNKNOWN"],"countries":[],"impressions":{"text":null,"index":-1},"spend":null,"creative":{"bodyText":"If you work out and are not using NMES technology, you are simply at a huge disadvantage. Here’s why\n\nIt’s simple. Neuromuscular Electrical Stimulation(NMES) gives you control over the intensity of muscle contractions.\n\nAnd I know NMES technology sounds like a buzz word so let me explain how it works.\n\nSimply put: Muscles contract in reaction to electrical currents from our nerves, and depending on how much the nerve is firing changes what muscle fibers are recruited.\n\nThis is in no way a shortcut to getting stronger, faster, and more toned. But having the ability to contract muscles at the optimal intensity of your choosing is a great advantage to have.\n\nThe results? An 8-week study on Muscle Stimulators led by industry-leading NMES scientist Dr. Toshio Moritani, Ph.D. found stellar results:\n\n✓ Waist circumference decreased by 4.48 cm\n✓ 59% increase in abdominal strength\n✓ 42% increase on max duration when holding a plank position\n✓ 121% increase in abdominal endurance\n✓ 74% felt that their posture had improved\n✓ 100% of the NMES group felt that their midsections were more toned and firmed\n\n“The NMES offers a promising alternative to traditional strength training for enhancing the strength parameters and motor abilities described above. Because of the clear-cut advantages in time management, we can expect this method to see the increasing use in high-performance sports.” -Dr. Toshio Moritani, Ph.D.\n\nShop Now to Get Yours While It's Still 49% OFF + FREE Worldwide Shipping!","title":"SALE ENDS TODAY!","caption":"abstimulator.news","linkUrl":"https://abstimulator.news/pages/t5-abs-stimulator","linkDescription":"Do Ab Stimulators Actually Work? We Tested 14 to Find Out. We expected to debunk the whole category. The technology turned out to be real. Most of the products aren't.","callToAction":"Shop now","callToActionType":"SHOP_NOW","displayFormat":"IMAGE","images":[{"url":"https://scontent-lga3-2.xx.fbcdn.net/v/t39.35426-6/791227723_1082641324295257_4249794444817469427_n.jpg?_nc_cat=101&ccb=1-7&_nc_sid=c53f8f&_nc_ohc=Fa2PdlpTQvkQ7kNvwFXvQcl&_nc_oc=AdrEALLEI25Q7AqcGbCgh0AEPF6snGaNkcoFKjNYFQIbiFTGAGH624HjYe0JxXGF0Nk&_nc_zt=14&_nc_ht=scontent-lga3-2.xx&_nc_gid=KAtc36otxCMlEdXH4WFHJA&_nc_ss=78180&oh=00_AQReJxmtve3diyq0_fooIaPI-xsI-naRBoRjBPiZk3APOg&oe=6AF3BD68","resizedUrl":"https://scontent-lga3-1.xx.fbcdn.net/v/t39.35426-6/788550125_2217683138792295_8323150730045197336_n.jpg?stp=dst-jpg_s600x600_tt6&_nc_cat=110&ccb=1-7&_nc_sid=c53f8f&_nc_ohc=90Zf1KmQ6zUQ7kNvwFRFr01&_nc_oc=AdpagFxK3xqtxmtP1-O0KmYj0T3rQ5MLD6BLvld-Dwev0ymTL48rAL_BCnUHEBCAqHQ&_nc_zt=14&_nc_ht=scontent-lga3-1.xx&_nc_gid=KAtc36otxCMlEdXH4WFHJA&_nc_ss=78180&oh=00_AQTdfklm0qtAFjlnBs42JGdzpD62-u1u-NRuugOcKd1d4A&oe=6AF3C9D5","watermarkedResizedUrl":null}],"videos":[],"cards":[]},"brandedContent":null,"euTransparency":null},{"id":"1068822359098456","adId":null,"url":"https://www.facebook.com/ads/library?id=1068822359098456","page":{"id":"1309935158872348","name":"She Tones","url":"https://www.facebook.com/61594893895516/","isDeleted":false,"profilePictureUrl":"https://scontent-lga3-1.xx.fbcdn.net/v/t39.35426-6/821295437_1088469690708718_96532495227500959_n.jpg?stp=dst-jpg_s60x60_tt6&_nc_cat=103&ccb=1-7&_nc_sid=c53f8f&_nc_ohc=zsSWsOCV-tUQ7kNvwEi-GL9&_nc_oc=Adogx-3yvPpR-cBSn5sya5ZvXnmxGsD_iGRV7PXyTeP_X31ok9wp-H2HGp73MUkpJww&_nc_zt=14&_nc_ht=scontent-lga3-1.xx&_nc_gid=KAtc36otxCMlEdXH4WFHJA&_nc_ss=78180&oh=00_AQRdUUSpiOOL4tou2MI0UyyrPiSVy3xSRmW_xahueXTW2w&oe=6AF3BD78","likeCount":3932,"categories":["Sports & Recreation"]},"campaign":{"collationId":"1643842873946442","collationCount":1},"isActive":true,"publisherPlatforms":["FACEBOOK","INSTAGRAM","AUDIENCE_NETWORK","WHATSAPP","THREADS"],"startedAt":"2026-09-25T07:00:00.000Z","endedAt":"2026-11-06T08:00:00.000Z","categories":["UNKNOWN"],"countries":[],"impressions":{"text":null,"index":-1},"spend":null,"creative":{"bodyText":"If you want to lift and tone your glutes and you're not using NMES technology, you're at a serious disadvantage. Here's why.\n\nIt comes down to control. Neuromuscular Electrical Stimulation (NMES) gives you precise control over the intensity of every muscle contraction, something squats and lunges simply can't replicate.\n\nAnd I know NMES sounds like a buzzword, so let me break it down.\n\nYour muscles contract in response to electrical signals from your nerves. The stronger the signal, the more muscle fibers get recruited. NMES sends those signals directly into the muscle, bypassing the limits of effort, form, and fatigue that hold most workouts back.\n\nThis isn't a shortcut to a sculpted lower body. But having the ability to fire your glutes at the exact intensity you choose — for hundreds of contractions per session — is a massive advantage traditional training can't match.\n\nThe results? In just one 20-minute session with the Ultra Glute Stimulator:\n\n✓ 600+ deep glute contractions, the equivalent of 3,000+ squats\n✓ Direct activation of the gluteus maximus and medius (the muscles that lift and shape)\n✓ Zero strain on your knees or lower back\n✓ Reaches deep muscle fibers most workouts never touch\n✓ Fully hands-free —train while you work, cook, or relax\n✓ No pads, no gels, no maintenance, ever\n\nNMES isn't some gimmick either. It's been studied for decades and endorsed by some of the world's leading researchers. As Dr. Toshio Moritani, Ph.D., a pioneer in NMES science, put it:\n\n\"The NMES offers a promising alternative to traditional strength training for enhancing the strength parameters and motor abilities described above. Because of the clear-cut advantages in time management, we can expect this method to see the increasing use in high-performance sports.\"\n\nThat same technology — trusted in clinical rehab and elite athletic training — is now engineered specifically for your glutes inside the Ultra Glute Stimulator.","title":"SALE ENDS TODAY!","caption":"apebornfitness.com","linkUrl":"https://apebornfitness.com/products/nextgen-ultra-glute-stimulator","linkDescription":null,"callToAction":"Shop now","callToActionType":"SHOP_NOW","displayFormat":"DCO","images":[],"videos":[],"cards":[{"title":"SALE ENDS TODAY!","body":"If you want to lift and tone your glutes and you're not using NMES technology, you're at a serious disadvantage. Here's why.\n\nIt comes down to control. Neuromuscular Electrical Stimulation (NMES) gives you precise control over the intensity of every muscle contraction, something squats and lunges simply can't replicate.\n\nAnd I know NMES sounds like a buzzword, so let me break it down.\n\nYour muscles contract in response to electrical signals from your nerves. The stronger the signal, the more muscle fibers get recruited. NMES sends those signals directly into the muscle, bypassing the limits of effort, form, and fatigue that hold most workouts back.\n\nThis isn't a shortcut to a sculpted lower body. But having the ability to fire your glutes at the exact intensity you choose — for hundreds of contractions per session — is a massive advantage traditional training can't match.\n\nThe results? In just one 20-minute session with the Ultra Glute Stimulator:\n\n✓ 600+ deep glute contractions, the equivalent of 3,000+ squats\n✓ Direct activation of the gluteus maximus and m